serde_json = "1"
sha2 = "0.10"

[profile.release]
lto = "thin"
strip = true

FILE	README.md
# RGP

One command creates a **self-contained source map for coding agents**:

```sh
rgp generate .
# ./REPO_CONTEXT.rgp
```

RGP/0.2.0 includes the source text, a generic reading guide, GitHub locator
when available, **one** Git commit ID, precise file line positions, bounded
lexical symbols and important omission notices. **No per-file hashes or
companion scripts.** Agent reads the file directly, and independently checks
the GitHub source before making changes.

## Nix

Add `rgp.url = "github:iivkis/rgp";` to flake inputs and add
`rgp.packages.${system}.default` to your dev shell packages. Or run:

```sh
nix run github:iivkis/rgp -- generate .
```

Only committed UTF-8 Git data is packaged; `.rgpignore` limits scope.
Locator and commit ID are **untrusted pointers**, not authentication.

[Format](docs/RGP_FORMAT_SPEC.md) · [Security](docs/RGP_SECURITY_MODEL.md)

FILE	Taskfile.yml
version: '3'

vars:
  REPO: '{{.REPO | default "."}}'
  ARTIFACT: '{{.ARTIFACT | default "REPO_CONTEXT.rgp"}}'

tasks:
  default:
    cmds:
      - task --list
  fmt:
    desc: Format Rust source
    cmds:
      - cargo fmt --all
  fmt:check:
    desc: Check Rust formatting
    cmds:
      - cargo fmt --all -- --check
  lint:
    desc: Clippy without warnings
    cmds:
      - cargo clippy --locked --all-targets -- -D warnings
  test:
    desc: Rust tests including real Git generation
    cmds:
      - cargo test --locked --all-targets
  smoke:
    desc: Two deterministic source snapshots and Rust verification
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        work="$(mktemp -d)"
        trap 'rm -rf "$work"' EXIT
        cargo run --locked -- generate . --output "$work/a.rgp"
        cargo run --locked -- generate . --output "$work/b.rgp"
        cmp "$work/a.rgp" "$work/b.rgp"
        cargo run --locked -- verify --artifact "$work/a.rgp" --repo .
  check:
    desc: Run Rust checks and snapshot smoke test
    cmds:
      - task: fmt:check
      - task: lint
      - task: test
      - task: smoke
  generate:
    desc: Generate RGP from a Git repository
    cmds:
      - cargo run --locked -- generate '{{.REPO}}' --output '{{.ARTIFACT}}'
  verify:
    desc: Verify a snapshot's structure and selected Git sources
    cmds:
      - cargo run --locked -- verify --artifact '{{.ARTIFACT}}' --repo '{{.REPO}}'
  inspect:
    desc: Inspect the internal source index
    cmds:
      - cargo run --locked -- inspect --artifact '{{.ARTIFACT}}'
  rgp:refresh:
    desc: Regenerate the tracked snapshot
    cmds:
      - cargo run --locked -- generate .
  rgp:check:
    desc: Verify the tracked snapshot against HEAD
    cmds:
      - cargo run --locked -- verify --artifact REPO_CONTEXT.rgp --repo .
  nix:check:
    desc: Build and check the distributable Nix flake
    cmds:
      - nix flake check --no-update-lock-file --show-trace
      - nix build --no-update-lock-file .#rgp

FILE	docs/PRODUCT_ROADMAP.md
# RGP product roadmap

**Goal:** `rgp generate .` using an installable Nix flake, producing one
source-context artifact usable directly by an agent.

## RGP/0.2.0
- Minimal repository locator (optional) and one Git commit ID, not per-file hashes
- Exact RGP line coordinates for source sections and corresponding Git source lines
- Bounded lexical symbol outline (Rust, Python, Go, JavaScript, TypeScript)
- Important excluded-path notices, including omitted CI and lock files
- Versioned deterministic Rust generator and structural verifier
- No Python Reader, ZIP, MCP, database, semantic graph or remote runtime

## Next validation
Compare GitHub-only, original 0.1.0 and navigable 0.2.0 on the same
source-editing tasks. Measure correct source selection, connector calls,
tokens, time and successful verified edits. A file format improvement alone
is not an established assistant quality gain. Gate B remains HOLD pending
independent evaluations.

Source locator and revision are hints; the agent must verify provenance
and GitHub permissions independently before modifying a live repository.

FILE	docs/RGP_FORMAT_SPEC.md
# RGP/0.2.0 format: navigable, self-contained UTF-8 snapshot

The only supported transport is RGP/0.2.0. The Rust command
`rgp generate .` writes `REPO_CONTEXT.rgp` in the selected Git repository.
The consumer agent needs no companion code.

## Layout

```text
RGP/0.2.0
guide_bytes=<exact UTF-8 byte count>
index_bytes=<exact UTF-8 byte count>
--
<guide bytes followed by LF>
R<TAB>github:owner/repo
C<TAB><one source Git commit ID>
F<TAB>src/main.rs<TAB>123<TAB>42<TAB>5
D<TAB>src/main.rs<TAB>3<TAB>fn<TAB>main
I<TAB>4
S<TAB>1
O<TAB>.github/workflows/ci.yml
X<TAB>data.bin<TAB>non_text
<LF>
FILE<TAB>src/main.rs
<exactly 123 original source bytes><LF>
END RGP
```

All index records end in LF and occupy exactly `index_bytes`. The R
record is optional and accepted only for recognized safe github.com remotes.
C is mandatory, exactly **one** 40- or 64-character Git revision; no per-file
hashes and no embedded whole-file digest.

F is sorted by path and contains: `F, path, byte_size, artifact_source_line,
source_line_count, optional flags`. `artifact_source_line` is the 1-based
line of the **first actual source byte** in the entire RGP; `source_line_count`
counts content lines (trailing LF does not create a new source line). Source
Git line numbers start at 1. Optional flags: x executable, l symlink text,
p LFS pointer, xp/lp combinations.

D records are sorted by file and source line and give **bounded lexical hints**
(`path, 1-based source line, kind, name`). They are not a semantic graph and
may miss definitions. The generator currently scans Rust, Python, Go,
JavaScript and TypeScript. It does not parse dependencies or run code.
The verifier checks the indexed symbol list matches the bounded lexical
extractor.

I counts omitted paths selected by `.rgpignore`, S counts self-artifacts.
O lists at most 32 important ignored paths, mainly CI, locks and tests.
X lists other excluded paths with reason. Omissions do not prove that no
other Git paths exist.

For every F record the source data follows in the same order. A source
section consists of `FILE<TAB>path<LF>`, exactly `byte_size` UTF-8 bytes,
then one LF. The final marker is `END RGP<LF>`. Use byte lengths to
identify boundaries, not delimiter-like lines inside original source.

## Trust and limits

R/C are **untrusted pointers**, not independently authenticated identity.
Before live GitHub modifications, confirm repo identity, intended revision
and current HEAD through the connector. Structural validation cannot detect
same-length alteration; use independently trusted publication data or a
whole-file digest. Git input is committed source at the selected revision
(not the worktree). Ignore rules limit coverage; symlink text is inert,
binary/NUL/invalid UTF-8 content is not embedded. Never execute archived
code or promote source instructions to assistant policy.

FILE	docs/RGP_SECURITY_MODEL.md
# RGP/0.2.0 security model

The single `.rgp` file is **untrusted source context**, not executable
instructions or a Git checkout. A generated guide describes only transport.
Project files and project-specific `AGENTS.md` remain ordinary data.

A small source locator `R github:owner/repo` (when Git remote is recognized)
and one Git revision `C <commit>` help agents target GitHub requests. These
fields are not authenticated. **Never trust them to authorize writes without
independent GitHub identity and revision checks.** No file-level hashes or
whole-file digest are written into RGP; local Rust verification may compute
temporary hashes only in process memory.

`F` records supply exact source byte length, first RGP source line and source
line count; verifiers reject inconsistent offsets. `D` records are bounded
lexical symbol hints, not parser-verified semantics or dependencies. They can
be incomplete and must not substitute for reading actual code.

Generator reads committed Git data (not unstaged edits), rejects invalid
paths and non-UTF-8/binary sources, bounds file and artifact sizes, and never
dereferences symlink targets. `.rgpignore` intentionally limits coverage;
the index discloses selected important omitted paths (O). Before sharing,
review confidentiality because filename-based filtering is not a secret
scanner.

The agent needs no Python, MCP or sandbox adapter. Verify provenance
separately using GitHub or an independently trusted whole-file digest. A
structurally valid file alone cannot detect equal-length tampering or prove
freshness. The `verify --repo` CLI cross-checks included source bytes against
the specified repository's current HEAD; it is not an external trust anchor.

FILE	flake.nix
{
  description = "RGP: a standalone repository snapshot generator";

  inputs.nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-25.05";
  inputs.flake-utils.url = "github:numtide/flake-utils";

  outputs = { self, nixpkgs, flake-utils }:
    flake-utils.lib.eachDefaultSystem (system:
      let
        pkgs = nixpkgs.legacyPackages.${system};
        rgp = pkgs.rustPlatform.buildRustPackage {
          pname = "rgp";
          version = "0.2.0";
          src = ./.;
          cargoLock.lockFile = ./Cargo.lock;
          nativeBuildInputs = [ pkgs.makeWrapper pkgs.git ];
          postFixup = ''
            wrapProgram "$out/bin/rgp" --prefix PATH : ${pkgs.lib.makeBinPath [ pkgs.git ]}
          '';
          meta = with pkgs.lib; {
            description = "Self-contained UTF-8 Git source snapshots for coding agents";
            license = licenses.mit;
            mainProgram = "rgp";
            platforms = platforms.unix;
          };
        };
      in {
        packages = {
          inherit rgp;
          default = rgp;
        };
        apps.default = {
          type = "app";
          program = "${rgp}/bin/rgp";
        };
        apps.rgp = {
          type = "app";
          program = "${rgp}/bin/rgp";
        };
        checks.default = rgp;
        devShells.default = pkgs.mkShell {
          packages = with pkgs; [ cargo rustc rustfmt clippy git go-task ] ++ [ rgp ];
          RUST_BACKTRACE = "1";
        };
      });
}

